---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const RECENT_SLUGS: Array<[string, string]> = [
  ['places', 'the-hearth'],
  ['places', 'the-wilds'],
  ['eras', 'age-of-tapestry'],
  ['eras', 'the-dark-century'],
  ['concepts', 'the-creeping-dark'],
  ['concepts', 'the-five-filters-of-uniqueness'],
  ['events', 'the-first-descent'],
  ['organizations', 'the-council'],
  ['people', 'the-longs'],
];

const all = await Promise.all([
  getCollection('places'),
  getCollection('eras'),
  getCollection('concepts'),
  getCollection('events'),
  getCollection('organizations'),
  getCollection('people'),
  getCollection('objects'),
  getCollection('language'),
]);
const flat = all.flat();
const lookup = new Map(flat.map((e) => [`${e.collection}/${e.slug}`, e]));

const recent = RECENT_SLUGS
  .map(([col, slug]) => lookup.get(`${col}/${slug}`))
  .filter((e): e is NonNullable<typeof e> => Boolean(e))
  .map((e) => ({
    collection: e.collection,
    slug: e.slug,
    name: 'name' in e.data ? e.data.name : (e.data as { word: string }).word,
    kahu_tok: 'kahu_tok' in e.data ? e.data.kahu_tok : undefined,
    summary: 'summary' in e.data ? e.data.summary : (e.data as { definition?: string }).definition ?? '',
  }));
---

<Layout>
  <h1>an archive of <span class="proper">tora vyl drak</span></h1>

  <p class="lede">
    a sanctuary built inside a volcanic caldera, high in the bones of the cascade range, twenty-five hundred years after the sky fell. its people, its places, its language, and the long quiet history that shaped them.
  </p>

  <hr class="kahu-rule" />

  <p>
    in the year 4625 of the old calendar, the <span class="proper">kahu</span> live inside an eighteen mile caldera in the cascade range. they call their home <span class="proper">tora vyl drak</span>, literally <em>hope, call, last</em>: the hope of the last call. the name was earned. in the year 2075, a seven kilometer asteroid on a collision course with earth was struck by the combined nuclear arsenals of the world's superpowers in a final attempt to redirect it. the strike broke the asteroid in two. it did not turn it. a three kilometer fragment came down in the atlantic and erased europe and the eastern seaboard. a four kilometer fragment struck the juan de fuca plate off the cascadia coast, triggered a megathrust earthquake that flooded the willamette valley, and the plasma trail of its passage generated a global emp that ended the age of electricity. half the world died in the first hours. nine in ten of the survivors died in the hyper-winter that followed.
  </p>

  <p>
    then came the slow part. the fallout poisoned what the impacts had spared, and over the centuries a fungal organism spread across the wounded surface of the world: <span class="kt">peli-shen</span>, <em>danger-life</em>. <span class="kt">peli-shen</span> is not a fast death. its airborne spores accumulate in the body as heavy metals do, and the first thing to go is the mind. survivors below the spore line grew slower, then strange, then unwell, then gone. the kahu call this long descent the creeping dark. the fungus thrives below five thousand feet and falters above it. the caldera floor sits at six thousand. a margin, not a generous one.
  </p>

  <p>
    inside the rim, the <span class="proper">kahu</span> are roughly two hundred and seventy-eight thousand people, woven into a tapestry of smaller kahu, tending each other and the systems that keep them alive. within the community there are vocations. the warden-tenders care for the living systems, including the viral and bacterial agents that make daily life possible. the <span class="proper">zou-esh</span>, the small and devoted order of scholar-warriors who survive the training, leave the sanctuary on long missions: searching for survivors, gathering supplies, recording what the world below the rim has become. across the centuries, the survivors the zou-esh have brought home are the threads from which the tapestry is woven.
  </p>

  <p>
    this is the encyclopedia of that world. it is being written, slowly, by hand. the voice here is objective, a record. stories told from inside the world live elsewhere.
  </p>

  <h2>browse</h2>

  <div class="browse">
    <a href="/people">
      <span class="label">people</span>
      <span class="meta">founders, figures, the named</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/places">
      <span class="label">places</span>
      <span class="meta">the caldera and beyond</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/events">
      <span class="label">events</span>
      <span class="meta">the fracture, the leveling, the schism</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/eras">
      <span class="label">eras</span>
      <span class="meta">tapestry, bloom, endura</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/concepts">
      <span class="label">concepts</span>
      <span class="meta">peli-shen, warden, the cascade</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/language">
      <span class="label">language</span>
      <span class="meta">kahu-tok and the bixel 1000</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/organizations">
      <span class="label">organizations</span>
      <span class="meta">zou-esh, the council, the tenders</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/objects">
      <span class="label">objects</span>
      <span class="meta">the zou-kit and beyond</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <h2>recently added</h2>

  <ul class="recently-added">
    {recent.map((r) => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/${r.collection}/${r.slug}`}>
          <span class="recently-added-name">{r.name}</span>
          {r.kahu_tok && <span class="kt recently-added-kt">{r.kahu_tok}</span>}
          <span class="recently-added-collection">{r.collection}</span>
        </a>
        {r.summary && <p class="recently-added-summary">{r.summary}</p>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>about this archive</h2>

  <p>
    this site is a work in progress. entries are being moved here from the master notes one at a time, with care. cross-links between entries are live where you see them. the ember-colored underlines mark proper nouns under the <span class="kt">kahu-tok</span> writing convention, and words set in <span class="kt">monospaced italic</span> are kahu-tok terms.
  </p>

  <p>
    if you find this place: welcome. <span class="kt">micasu</span>.
  </p>
</Layout>
